   "id": "bava_batra.52a.5",
   "daf": "52a",
   "sentenceId": 4,
   "he": "מִן הַקָּטָן – יַעֲשֶׂה לוֹ סְגוּלָּה. מַאי ״סְגוּלָּה״? רַב חִסְדָּא אָמַר: סֵפֶר תּוֹרָה. רַבָּה בַּר רַב הוּנָא אָמַר: דִּיקְלָא דְּאָכֵל מִינֵּיהּ תַּמְרֵי.",
   "en": "The baraita stated that if the bailee took a deposit «from a minor, he must make a safe investment for him.» The Gemara asks: «What» is meant by «a safe investment? Rav Ḥisda says:» The bailee should purchase «a Torah scroll» for the minor. «Rabba bar Rav Huna says:» He should purchase «a date palm, from which» the minor «will consume dates.»"
  }
 ],
